# Two optional helpers are python3 scripts, and neither is worth a hard
# dependency on the interpreter in a thin client image.
#
# jetpipe is a printer daemon for clients with a printer attached, and
# ltsp-shadow-ui draws the two windows ltsp-shadow shows the user - the
# question before anyone may watch, and the marker while they do. Sites that
# want either install the packages this one suggests; sites that do not would
# otherwise carry python3 and its standard library over NBD on every boot for
# a file they never run.
#
# Both say what is missing when they are started without it, rather than
# failing in a way that has to be guessed at.
ltsp-client-core: python3-script-but-no-python3-dep * [usr/sbin/jetpipe]
ltsp-client-core: python3-script-but-no-python3-dep * [usr/share/ltsp/ltsp-shadow-ui]
